k_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000149115","entrez_id":["85456"],"uniprot":["Q9C0C2"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables ankyrin repeat binding activity and enzyme binding activity. Involved in cellular response to ionizing radiation; double-strand break repair; and positive regulation of protein phosphorylation. Located in several cellular components, including actin cytoskeleton; adherens junction; and heterochromatin. Part of CCR4-NOT complex. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9C0C2","text":"Component of the CCR4-NOT complex, a large multiprotein complex with several proteins assembled around the scaffolding protein CNOT1 (PubMed:29593045, PubMed:31180491). This complex is one of the major cellular mRNA deadenylase and is linked to various cellular processes including bulk mRNA degradation, miRNA-mediated repression, translational repression during translational initiation and general transcription regulation. CNOT12 affects helicase selection into the CCR4-NOT complex (PubMed:29593045, PubMed:31180491). In addition, plays a role in DNA double strand break repair and is involved in actin cytoskeleton rearrangement and cancer cell invasion (PubMed:25749521, PubMed:28202517)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}